{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U41", "U44"],
      "pins": ["U41.5", "U44.5", "U41.8", "U44.8"],
      "nets": ["GND", "5V_switched_CAN"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U41 and U44 have their secondary-side ground pins (GND2, pin 5) connected to the system GND net, and their secondary-side supply pins (VCC2, pin 8) connected to the system-derived 5V_switched_CAN net.",
      "expected": "The specification states two isolated CAN buses through isolated CAN transceivers; an isolated transceiver's GND2/VCC2 must be a separate isolated secondary supply/ground, not tied to the primary GND/system rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U41\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U44\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U41\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller ... through an isolated CAN transceiver"}
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation of both CAN buses is defeated; CAN grounds are common with the board ground, causing ground loops and removing the intended isolation from the motor controllers.",
      "confidence": 0.93
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D4", "D12", "D28"],
      "pins": ["D4.2", "D12.2", "D28.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0076"],
      "observed": "The anodes of D4, D12, and D28 are tied together on net /NET0076, and that net has no other nodes: it is not connected to a supply, pull-up, or driver.",
      "expected": "Indicator LEDs must have their anodes connected to a positive supply or current source (e.g., +3V3) so the cathode-side drivers can sink current and light them.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"17\") (name \"/NET0076\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D12\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D28\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "These three status/Ethernet LEDs will not illuminate under any driver state because their common anode net is floating.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show a clear isolation defect: U41/U44 isolated CAN transceiver secondary grounds are tied to system GND, contradicting the intended isolated CAN buses. A secondary issue is that D4/D12/D28 share a floating anode net with no supply or driver, leaving those LEDs inoperative."
}

